{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And YHWH.</b> Everywhere 'וַהֳ' is said, it means He and His court — for the vav is a term of addition, as in 'so-and-so and so-and-so.'" "<b>Smote every firstborn.</b> Even those of another nation, as long as they were in Egypt (Mekhilta)." "<b>The firstborn of Pharaoh.</b> Pharaoh himself was also a firstborn, and he survived from among the firstborns — and about him it says ״בַּעֲבוּר הַרְאוֹתְךָ אֶת כֹּחִי״ (Exodus 9) — at the Sea of Reeds (Mekhilta)." "<b>Unto the firstborn of the captive.</b> For they rejoiced at Israel's calamity; and further, so they would not say 'our fear brought the punishment upon us'; and the firstborn of the maidservant was included, for he counts from the most distinguished among them all down to the lowliest — and the firstborn of the maidservant is more distinguished than the firstborn of the captive."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:46.731905906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}